WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
(audience applauding)
- I'm so excited you're here!

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.714
- I'm so excited to see you.

00:00:03.714 --> 00:00:05.200
It's been a few years.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.720
- It has, but I have to start with this.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.791
Okay, so "Bite Me" comes out,

00:00:07.791 --> 00:00:09.750
with Travis, the single,

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.880
and I see the video

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.120
and I'm like, were you in
some kind of time capsule?

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.802
'Cause you look just like you did.

00:00:17.802 --> 00:00:20.030
(audience applauding)
I was like, what?

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.340
I was literally watching it

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.360
and you did such a great job of like,

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.290
you know, people love your sound so much

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.940
and I felt like you did such a great job

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.440
of like having the sound
that we love you for

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.540
but it was progressive.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.220
Like it was different and it was so,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.390
anyway job, well done.
- Aww.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.479
Thank you so much!
- All the way round.

00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:36.237
I was like, God.
(audience applauding)

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:38.082
And I love "Bite Me." It was so good.

00:00:38.082 --> 00:00:39.292
- Thank you.
- I was so excited about it

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:41.790
and what a way to like, just
come swinging with a single.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.080
Anyway, I just wanted to say that.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.180
And I didn't know this

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.671
but you started out in country music?

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:47.290
Or that was your first-
- Kind of.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.100
Like I started singing in
church when I was younger

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.510
and then like I sang with
Shania Twain when I was like 14

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.343
on stage-
- What?

00:00:55.343 --> 00:00:57.470
- And just like country fairs around town.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.899
Then when I got into
high school, I was like,

00:00:58.899 --> 00:00:59.880
(Avril squeaking)

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.740
and like started writing my own stuff

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.120
and developing my sound then

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.070
and went off to kind of make my record.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.580
But yeah. Yeah.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.650
- Well, this year is
actually the 20th anniversary

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.130
of your album, "Let Go."

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.420
What do you remember about making it?

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.830
'Cause people ask me,

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.180
I've been in the industry
about 20 years too

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.290
and it's like-
- Yeah.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.340
- I think how people
perceive things is different

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.173
than maybe,

00:01:20.173 --> 00:01:22.210
there's a lot of good and bad
that goes on behind the scenes

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.150
while making a record.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.770
- Like what do you remember about it?

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.680
- Well, I think making
my first record was hard

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.970
because like I wanted to be a songwriter

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.130
and I was 15

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.190
and like people didn't really like,

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:34.270
like I'd go in the studio

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.780
and they were just like,
"Yeah, yeah, yeah, little girl.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.643
Like you don't know what you're like."

00:01:36.643 --> 00:01:37.690
You know what I mean?
- Oh yeah, I got that too.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.283
- And it was kind of like
they were throwing their songs

00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:43.060
at me and pitching their songs to me,

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.700
which I really didn't like.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.310
And so it was a fight.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:47.760
It was a fight to write my own music

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.470
and then it was a fight
to get the sound I wanted

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.390
'cause like I guess like I was
going for like guitar driven-

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.223
- Yeah.
- Like music.

00:01:54.223 --> 00:01:55.930
I was like, "I just
wanna sound like a band.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:56.763
I wanna rock."

00:01:56.763 --> 00:01:58.680
And that was my challenge.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.840
And so it took like,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.440
I was in New York maybe six months,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.550
working with tons of writers.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.230
It just was not happening.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.830
And then I went through a point

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.940
where I think it just like
wasn't working out very great.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.220
And then I went to LA,

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.390
and then I finally met with some people,

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.277
producers and co-writers
that like listened to me.

00:02:15.277 --> 00:02:17.790
And I, at that point had tried so hard

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.700
and I was like developing
into like who I wanted to be.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.533
And it worked.

00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:22.840
I found people I clicked with.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.090
And so like, yeah.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.640
Like that album took a
while and it was hard

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.190
and I had to like fight for
like being a songwriter,

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.190
fight to like have the
sound that I wanted,

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.150
sit with the producers.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.288
I had no idea what the lingo was.

00:02:34.288 --> 00:02:35.970
I was just like, "Make it more rock.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.330
Make it sound more like a band."

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.980
But what I wanted just
was guitar driven stuff.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.090
I think it would've been
more polished and poppy

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.020
and bubble gum and that
wasn't what I wanted.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:44.870
So-
- Yeah.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.900
- I made the record I did want though.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.733
- I love that.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:48.880
And it is true though.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.300
You have to like-
- After all that.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.133
- People push,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.130
especially in the
beginning of my career too,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.367
they push and you're a
teenager and they're like,

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:54.200
"Oh we're gonna make,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.416
you know, write with this person do this."

00:02:55.416 --> 00:02:56.624
And it's like, you don't
click with everyone.

00:02:56.624 --> 00:02:57.512
- Yeah.
- And there's nothing wrong

00:02:57.512 --> 00:02:58.400
with them.
- No.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.233
- But like-
- Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:02:59.233 --> 00:03:00.200
- You do find your people

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.510
that you click really well with.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.220
And then I feel like magic happens, so.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.053
- Yeah, for sure.

00:03:04.053 --> 00:03:04.886
- Yeah.

00:03:04.886 --> 00:03:06.080
Well I love all your albums, so-

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:06.930
- Thank you.
- I'm so excited

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.763
about this one.

00:03:07.763 --> 00:03:09.320
So as I mentioned though, your new album

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.240
is called "Love Sux,"

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.380
which well, sometimes it does.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.590
- Mm-hmm. Let's face it.
- But I heard,

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.490
ironically enough,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.717
that you met your new
boyfriend while making it?

00:03:16.717 --> 00:03:17.550
- How funny is that?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.020
Like I went into the studio,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:19.853
I'm literally like,

00:03:19.853 --> 00:03:20.686
(Avril sighing)

00:03:20.686 --> 00:03:21.860
"Okay, here's where I'm at.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.210
Like, I'm over love.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.220
I need a hot minute.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.800
Like I'm jaded on love right now, like."

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.633
- Flick.

00:03:28.633 --> 00:03:29.466
- Ugh.
- Yes.

00:03:29.466 --> 00:03:31.520
- And like, so you kind
of have to like do that

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.700
when you're in your writing sessions.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.130
Just talk about like
where you're at and stuff.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.289
So I wrote that song, "Love Sux."

00:03:35.289 --> 00:03:38.650
That set the tone for this album.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.483
Yeah.

00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:41.186
And then a couple days
later I had a boyfriend.

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:42.038
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:42.038 --> 00:03:44.179
That didn't last very long, did it, Avril?

00:03:44.179 --> 00:03:46.460
(audience applauding)

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.220
I'm literally never single.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.544
- I love, I know, but
I love that it's like,

00:03:49.544 --> 00:03:50.960
you're not wanting it.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:51.793
It wasn't even-
- Yeah, I know.

00:03:51.793 --> 00:03:52.626
- What you were searching for.

00:03:52.626 --> 00:03:54.070
- And it was like the
first time in my life,

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.690
like I had just like moved

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.230
and I moved out to Malibu

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.150
and was like starting my life over

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.990
and I was like, "All right, like I'm good.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.570
Like I'm just gonna focus
on myself and like do me

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.750
and just like give it a break."

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.330
Plus I haven't had like the best luck,

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.110
but I mean I've had amazing relationships

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.495
and they've been like long term.

00:04:13.495 --> 00:04:14.500
- Yeah.
- And stuff.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.490
But like I was just kinda like,

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.869
"Okay I'm gonna on myself."

00:04:17.869 --> 00:04:20.030
And it just like really didn't last.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:20.863
- It happens.

00:04:20.863 --> 00:04:21.696
And you were like, "Or
I'll go on this date."

00:04:21.696 --> 00:04:23.140
- Yeah, whatever.
- Well that was awesome.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.160
- But made an album called "Love Sux"

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.703
but it's also like super lighthearted

00:04:26.703 --> 00:04:28.620
and like funny and fun.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.343
And it's like kind of just
like the ups and downs

00:04:30.343 --> 00:04:32.870
of my life in love and just like,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.610
it's a good time and it's-
- Which is relatable.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.770
- Yeah. For sure.
- For a lot of people.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.590
- And like my first
album, it's like, yeah,

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.220
am I kind of still
writing in the same (beep)

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.215
but like,
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:40.215 --> 00:04:41.048
you know,

00:04:41.048 --> 00:04:43.580
it's like I was writing when
I got out of high school,

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.270
like fresh outta high school.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:48.342
Just like having crushes
for the first time.

00:04:48.342 --> 00:04:49.410
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.130
- And now on my seventh album,

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:55.039
it's like my, you know,
I've had experience,

00:04:55.039 --> 00:04:56.202
I've lived, I've learned

00:04:56.202 --> 00:04:58.247
and men don't change.
- But that's why I think

00:04:58.247 --> 00:04:59.938
it was a good thing though.
(Avril laughing)

00:04:59.938 --> 00:05:00.860
No, no, no!

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.818
No, apparently they stay the same.

00:05:02.818 --> 00:05:05.253
(Avril laughing)
No, but I think it's like,

00:05:05.253 --> 00:05:06.670
I think it was a good,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.270
like I said, I like that you
kept like the vibe was cool

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.980
and like similar to
what we love about you,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.240
but it wasn't the same.
- Yeah.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.610
- I think it's a really cool,

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.350
progressive like sound of it.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.250
So, or progressed sound of it, rather.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.280
But I love it.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.680
And I think it's relatable,

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.210
doesn't matter how old you are.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.960
We through ups and downs in relationships.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.120
- Yeah.
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.530
- It happens.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.860
But later in the show,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.527
you're gonna be doing a song called,

00:05:29.527 --> 00:05:30.660
"Love It When You Hate Me,"

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.990
which I love, that one as well.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:32.823
It's very sarcastic.

00:05:32.823 --> 00:05:33.860
So what's it about?
- Yeah!

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.830
It's like a fun, funny take on like,

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.770
like being in like a heated,
passionate relationship

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.085
where it's like, you know, you're fighting

00:05:41.085 --> 00:05:44.170
and then it's and hot and-
- Yeah.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.003
Yeah.

00:05:45.003 --> 00:05:46.130
And 'cause then you get the makeup stuff.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:46.963
- Yeah.
- So there you go.

00:05:46.963 --> 00:05:47.810
I kept it family-
- Love that.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:48.686
- Yeah.

00:05:48.686 --> 00:05:49.660
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.210
Well everybody, Avril's new
album is called "Love Sux."

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.230
You've gotta check it out

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.520
and stay with us because she's
performing later in the show.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.370
I'm super stoked!

